{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4481","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4481/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4481/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4481/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4481","id":4323973366,"node_id":"I_kwDOBM4HkM8AAAABAbqY9g","number":4481,"title":"AMF does not return ERROR INDICATION upon receiving INITIAL UE MESSAGE with an already‑used RAN UE NGAP ID","user":{"login":"se-prok","id":81800148,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODAwMTQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81800148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok","html_url":"https://github.com/se-prok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/se-prok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4586072876,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBM4HkM8AAAABEVnrLA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/labels/Type:Security","name":"Type:Security","color":"AA10D4","default":false,"description":"Security issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5166283890,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBM4HkM8AAAABM-88cg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/labels/Housekeeping:ToClose","name":"Housekeeping:ToClose","color":"006B75","default":false,"description":"Issues reviewed and closed. Old requests, issues which are not bug, feature or documentation request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-04-24T15:36:02Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T23:33:30Z","closed_at":"2026-06-23T23:33:30Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi!\n\n3GPP TS 38.413 mandates that an INITIAL UE MESSAGE must carry a unique RAN UE NGAP ID. If the NG‑RAN node reuses an already‑active RAN UE NGAP ID in a new INITIAL UE MESSAGE instead of using the UPLINK NAS TRANSPORT procedure, the AMF must detect a logical error (clause 10.4) and respond with an ERROR INDICATION message.\n\nBut the current AMF implementation does not send this indication.\n\nInteraction steps (after initial NG SETUP REQUEST and NG SETUP RESPONSE):\n1. NG-RAN sends to AMF the REGISTRATION REQUEST message using INITIAL UE MESSAGE. \n2. AMF sends to NG-RAN the IDENTITY REQUEST message using DOWNLINK NAS TRANSPORT.  \n3. NG-RAN sends to AMF the IDENTITY RESPONSE message using INITIAL UE MESSAGE  (instead of using UPLINK NAS TRANSPORT) -- with the same RAN UE NGAP ID as in the first INITIAL UE MESSAGE.\n4. AMF doesn't respond with any message (it writes to log: \"[amf] ERROR: Invalid 5GMM message type [92] (../src/amf/ngap-path.c:248)\").\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"h